@startuml chain-state-diagram
title Life-cycle of one registration chain (persisted in the facade's chain log)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

[*] --> STARTED : intent logged before any subsystem is called
STARTED --> REJECTED : A refuses (nothing committed)
STARTED --> PENDING_B : A committed
PENDING_B --> PENDING_C : B committed
PENDING_C --> COMPLETED : C committed,\nB confirmed, A consumed

STARTED --> COMPENSATING : unexpected failure / restart
PENDING_B --> COMPENSATING : B failed -> undo A\n(or restart)
PENDING_C --> COMPENSATING : C failed -> undo B, then A\n(or restart)
COMPLETED --> COMPENSATING : administrator cancels\n(undo C, B, A)
COMPENSATING --> COMPENSATED : every committed step undone,\nnewest first

PENDING_B --> COMPLETED : recovery roll-forward\n(disk shows A, B, C committed)
PENDING_C --> COMPLETED : recovery roll-forward
STARTED --> COMPLETED : recovery roll-forward

REJECTED --> [*]
COMPENSATED --> [*]
COMPLETED --> [*]
@enduml
